  "summary": "Reclassify Stop After Current runtime evidence so Dashboard and Queue surfaces show an actionable hold plus a separate stopped progress bar instead of failed or blocked item states.",
  "reason": "Operator-requested Stop After Current currently looks like a failed Dashboard count and a blocked Queue row even when the pipeline obeyed the graceful stop request.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "queue",
    "status",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "A stopped runtime outcome could flow through status and Queue presentation as failed/blocked, and Home labeled the nonzero stop counter as Failed.",
  "behavior_after": "Explicit STOP_REQUESTED/stopped runtime evidence inserts a warning progress bar for the operator stop while Queue rows keep actionable next states such as Check publish state, Waiting for push, or Recently completed. Actual failed/error/blocked outcomes remain failure/blocker states.",
